(UR3E MANAGER-BASED CUBE STACKING TASK) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(MOTIVATION) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The UR3e manager-based stack task is intended to train a simulated Universal Robots UR3e arm) Tj
T*
(to stack three cubes on a table using a suction-style end effector. The task mirrors Isaac) Tj
T*
(Lab's manager-based manipulation stack examples, but adapts the robot, TCP frame, and reward) Tj
T*
(design to the local UR3e asset used in this repository.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The original Isaac Lab stack examples are well suited for imitation learning with robomimic) Tj
T*
(when demonstration data is available. In this project, no demonstration dataset is assumed.) Tj
T*
(For that reason, the task also exposes a `skrl` PPO entry point and includes shaped rewards) Tj
T*
(so that the policy can be trained from scratch.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The practical goal is to create a reusable sim training task for UR3e manipulation:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  * validate the local UR3e USD asset in a contact-rich tabletop scenario;) Tj
T*
(  * train a policy without manually collecting robomimic demonstrations;) Tj
T*
(  * keep compatibility with Isaac Lab's manager-based environment structure;) Tj
T*
(  * preserve a future path for behavior cloning if demonstrations are collected later.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(ENVIRONMENT DESCRIPTION) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The environment is registered as two Gym tasks:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  * `Isaac-Robots-Stack-Cube-UR3e-Long-Suction-IK-Rel-v0`) Tj
T*
(  * `Isaac-Robots-Stack-Cube-UR3e-Short-Suction-IK-Rel-v0`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Both tasks use `isaaclab.envs:ManagerBasedRLEnv` and the local manager-based UR3e stack) Tj
T*
(configuration. The difference between the two tasks is the suction offset used for the end) Tj
T*
(effector:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Variant  TCP body  Suction offset) Tj
T*
(Long suction  `tool0`  `0.22 m`) Tj
T*
(Short suction  `tool0`  `0.1585 m` / `0.159 m`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The scene contains:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  * one UR3e articulation loaded from the local `UR3E_CFG`;) Tj
T*
(  * one Seattle lab table;) Tj
T*
(  * three rigid cube objects: `cube_1`, `cube_2`, and `cube_3`;) Tj
T*
(  * a ground plane and dome light;) Tj
T*
(  * a `FrameTransformer` tracking the UR3e `tool0` TCP frame;) Tj
T*
(  * a surface gripper attached under `{ENV_REGEX_NS}/Robot/tool0/SurfaceGripper`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Isaac Lab's surface gripper backend currently requires CPU simulation, so the environment) Tj
T*
(sets both `self.device` and `self.sim.device` to `cpu`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(ACTION AND OBSERVATION SPACE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
