6 0 obj
<< /Length 2480 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 760 Td
14 TL
(The task uses relative differential inverse kinematics for arm motion:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  * arm action: relative end-effector pose command through) Tj
T*
(  `DifferentialInverseKinematicsActionCfg`;) Tj
T*
(  * gripper action: binary surface-gripper command through) Tj
T*
(  `SurfaceGripperBinaryActionCfg`;) Tj
T*
(  * IK body: `tool0`;) Tj
T*
(  * IK method: damped least squares \(`dls`\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For PPO, the policy observation group is configured with `concatenate_terms = True`. This) Tj
T*
(gives `skrl` a flat observation tensor instead of the dictionary-style observation layout) Tj
T*
(used by robomimic.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The policy observation contains:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  * previous action;) Tj
T*
(  * relative joint positions;) Tj
T*
(  * relative joint velocities;) Tj
T*
(  * stack object observation from Isaac Lab's stack MDP;) Tj
T*
(  * cube positions in world frame;) Tj
T*
(  * cube orientations in world frame;) Tj
T*
(  * end-effector position;) Tj
T*
(  * end-effector quaternion;) Tj
T*
(  * gripper position.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(REWARD DESIGN) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The PPO reward is intentionally shaped. Sparse success-only reward is unlikely to train) Tj
T*
(efficiently for a three-cube contact task from scratch, especially with a suction gripper) Tj
T*
(and no demonstrations. The reward therefore breaks the task into staged behaviors:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  1. approach `cube_2`;) Tj
T*
(  2. lift `cube_2`;) Tj
T*
(  3. align `cube_2` over `cube_1`;) Tj
T*
(  4. stack `cube_2` on `cube_1`;) Tj
T*
(  5. approach `cube_3`;) Tj
T*
(6. lift `cube_3`;) Tj
T*
(7. align `cube_3` over `cube_2`;) Tj
T*
(8. stack `cube_3` on `cube_2`;) Tj
T*
(9. award a full-stack success bonus.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The current reward terms are:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Reward term  Weight  Purpose) Tj
T*
(`reach_cube_2`  `2.0`  Move the TCP close to `cube_2`.) Tj
T*
(`lift_cube_2`  `4.0`  Lift `cube_2` above table height.) Tj
T*
(`align_cube_2_on_1`  `4.0`  Align `cube_2` horizontally above `cube_1`.) Tj
T*
(`stack_cube_2_on_1`  `10.0`  Reward a valid two-cube stack.) Tj
T*
(`reach_cube_3`  `1.0`  Move the TCP close to `cube_3`.) Tj
T*
(`lift_cube_3`  `3.0`  Lift `cube_3` above table height.) Tj
T*
(`align_cube_3_on_2`  `5.0`  Align `cube_3` horizontally above `cube_2`.) Tj
T*
(`stack_cube_3_on_2`  `15.0`  Reward placing the third cube on the stack.) Tj
T*
(`full_stack`  `30.0`  Reward the complete three-cube stack.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
